# Regression: scrolling the sidebar list used to leave the rows in place but
# stop drawing their titles past a certain offset — the rows stayed clickable
# and went blank.
#
# The list renders at most a viewport's worth of rows and offers the rest
# behind "Show N more…" (that cap is what keeps a 2000-session list cheap), and
# rows are 32px tall now, so at this window size the capped list FITS and there
# is nothing to scroll. Expanding it first is what gives the scroll something
# to move — which is also the state the regression appeared in.
#
# Both titles are asserted in their SIDEBAR-ellipsized form. Every row title is
# also painted on a Home card in the main pane, at a width that does not
# ellipsize it, and a duplicate label satisfies expect_text wherever it is —
# so a bare title would pass with every sidebar row blank, which is the exact
# regression this script exists for (afterhours_gaps.md #73). The "…" is what
# makes the assertion about the sidebar. "oncall sweep finished" is the
# thirteenth row: past the cap, so it is on screen only once the list has been
# expanded AND scrolled.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":[],"active_tab":"","theme":"dark"}

expect_text "stickers broke — concluded, D1136…"
expect_no_text "oncall sweep finished — 3 rows ne…"

click_ui sb_show_more
wait_frames 6

mouse_move 140 600
scroll_wheel 0 -6
wait_frames 6
scroll_wheel 0 -6
wait_frames 6

# Whatever is under the cursor now, SOMETHING must still be lettered: this row
# is far enough down the list to be on screen only after the scroll.
expect_text "oncall sweep finished — 3 rows ne…"
